      "id": "SIE-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "Rank-two volume and the level-index normalization",
      "anchor": "global-siegel-volume",
      "statement": "In the definite rank-two comparison, the normalized stabilizer K has measure one, the quotient fundamental domain has measure ∑ᵢ 1/|Γ∩gᵢKgᵢ⁻¹|, and the class and genus identifications make this the standard rank-two mass. The restricted-level subgroup has index [K:K′] and the word ratio uses row index / column index.",
      "hypotheses": "Countable rational unitary Γ, left-invariant normalized measure, measurable K, finite disjoint double-coset classes and finite stabilizers, and a Γ-fundamental domain. For the application: positive definite constant signature, volume tie, finite class representatives, stabilizer/automorphism correspondence and genus mass identified with standard mass at rank two.",
