      "correspondence": "For x∈Γg_iK, the translations into g_iK form a torsor for Γ∩g_iKg_i⁻¹. After division by the stabilizer order the periodized indicator is identically one on that class. Integration gives the reciprocal order for μ(K)=1. Any finite-index subgroup K′ has μ(K′)=1/[K:K′], explaining the larger factor on normalizing a deeper level to volume one. duStarP and DstarP multiply by idxPi and idxSig separately.",
      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "review": "Finite S₃ model with Γ=K=⟨(12)⟩ gives stabilizers 2 and 1, two double cosets of sizes 2 and 4 and volume 3/2 under μ(K)=1. Independent source review checked the normalization and that the rank-two definite input is the chosen base case."
    },
    {
      "id": "SIE-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "The Siegel increment from two limits and transfer to the indefinite row",
      "anchor": "global-siegel-increment",
      "statement": "For the chosen standard orthonormal lattices, the quotient mass_M/mass_(M−1) is {[(M−1)!(v/π)^M]^f/√((2v)^f)} Lη(M) for M≥3. The positive rank-one mass normalization cancels. The same normalized ratio for unit-vector complements propagates the definite rank-two identity to all constant signatures (P,Q) with P≥2 and hence to Y₀, whose dimension is r; the Count5 scale uses exactly k<M≤r.",
      "hypotheses": "E is an unramified CM field with fixed real field in the sense IsCMUnram, f=#infinite places=[E:ℚ]/2, v=|disc E|^(1/(2f))/2. In the mass recursion the Hermitian lattice is integral, totally positive definite, and spans a finite-dimensional E-space. The rank increment comparing orthonormal models is used at M≥3. The representation estimate invokes the binary Hermitian representation result and the pinned local density identity. For the indefinite transfer P≥2, the volume/measure tie and a signed norm-one orthogonal-complement volume formula hold. Thresholds and constants in other Count5 estimates are unchanged by this pointwise identity.",
