      "correspondence": "Normalize the weighted ball count at radius j by j^(2fM). Grouping nonzero vectors of the same length yields the representation mass sum, together with the zero-vector term. The lattice limit is μΛ(π^M/M!)^f/(v^(fM)δ). The local density limit is c_(M−1)λΛ M^(−f)Lη(M)/(δ√((2v)^f)). Cancel the nonzero δ and M^f in (M!)^f, obtaining the stated factorial and ratio. For an orthonormal lattice the λΛ-factors are all one. In the volume induction the complement of a norm +1 vector decreases P at Q=0, while a norm −1 vector decreases Q at fixed P≥2. For (P,Q)=sigY₀ their sum is r. The k-to-r telescope has m−1 increments.",
      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "review": "An independent reader checked both limiting coefficients, signs of the two inductions, f exponents and (M−1)! normalization. At M=3 and a finite prime of the real subfield with residue cardinality 2 the local Euler contribution is 8/9 in the inert case and 8/7 for a split pair. The two alternatives do not yield a numerical global mass."
