  "outstanding": [
    "The common positive rank-one mass constant is supplied by the rank-one theorem; its explicit absolute value is unnecessary for this ratio. The general weighted representation-density product, its asymptotic summation, local density identities and the binary Hermitian representation theorem are deeper arithmetic inputs.",
    "The rank-two genus classification, the adelic/unit-vector unfolding for the indefinite ratio and its real and finite local densities are traced to their suppliers. Their entire constructions and proofs are outside these two claims. The row induction used here requires P≥2 and a constant signature; no indefinite rank-one assertion is needed.",
    "The split and inert rank-three examples give local Euler factors conditional on splitting behaviour, and the finite S₃ quotient illustrates the measure identity. Neither computes the absolute genus mass of a selected host."
  ],
  "review_scope": "Independent readers reviewed the normalized double-coset formula, both limiting expressions for the common sequence, local Euler-factor example, positive/negative signature inductions and connection to Count5."
}
